{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-49256" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡3x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038169/state.json" "file_sha256" "294ac8a6312da67083ddee01c1c6d7e4ff3781621f176b6a7c44d36045e7e14e"} {"question" "q-49256" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡3x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡3x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡3x$ to express this as\n\n$$\n\\int {sec}^{2}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=3x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int {sec}^{2}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡u\\cdot \\,\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int {sec}^{2}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡3x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038169/state.json" "file_sha256" "294ac8a6312da67083ddee01c1c6d7e4ff3781621f176b6a7c44d36045e7e14e"} {"question" "q-49256" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038169/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ce191542b27f7f51d6b6ef778426f64d00c2b3bdc3edfb369c14f54dac6911a4"} {"question" "q-49256" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038169/state.json" "file_sha256" "294ac8a6312da67083ddee01c1c6d7e4ff3781621f176b6a7c44d36045e7e14e"} {"question" "q-49256" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡3x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}{sec}^{2}⁡3x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038169/state.json" "file_sha256" "294ac8a6312da67083ddee01c1c6d7e4ff3781621f176b6a7c44d36045e7e14e"} {"question" "q-49256" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡3x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038169/state.json" "file_sha256" "294ac8a6312da67083ddee01c1c6d7e4ff3781621f176b6a7c44d36045e7e14e"} {"question" "q-49273" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{{cos}^{3}⁡x+{cot}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038169/state.json" "file_sha256" "294ac8a6312da67083ddee01c1c6d7e4ff3781621f176b6a7c44d36045e7e14e"} {"question" "q-49273" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{{cos}^{3}⁡x+{cot}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}({cos}^{3}⁡x+{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that ${cot}^{2}⁡x=\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}$ to express this as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}({cos}^{3}⁡x+\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x})\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{cos}^{3}⁡x+{cot}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}({cos}^{3}⁡x+\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot {cos}^{3}⁡x+\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{csc}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038169/state.json" "file_sha256" "294ac8a6312da67083ddee01c1c6d7e4ff3781621f176b6a7c44d36045e7e14e"} {"question" "q-49273" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038169/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ce191542b27f7f51d6b6ef778426f64d00c2b3bdc3edfb369c14f54dac6911a4"} {"question" "q-49273" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038169/state.json" "file_sha256" "294ac8a6312da67083ddee01c1c6d7e4ff3781621f176b6a7c44d36045e7e14e"} {"question" "q-49273" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038169/state.json" "file_sha256" "294ac8a6312da67083ddee01c1c6d7e4ff3781621f176b6a7c44d36045e7e14e"} {"question" "q-49273" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038169/state.json" "file_sha256" "294ac8a6312da67083ddee01c1c6d7e4ff3781621f176b6a7c44d36045e7e14e"} {"question" "q-49281" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038169/state.json" "file_sha256" "294ac8a6312da67083ddee01c1c6d7e4ff3781621f176b6a7c44d36045e7e14e"} {"question" "q-49281" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡2x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThen, we use the identity $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡2x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡2x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let  $u=2x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.$ Hence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038169/state.json" "file_sha256" "294ac8a6312da67083ddee01c1c6d7e4ff3781621f176b6a7c44d36045e7e14e"} {"question" "q-49281" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038169/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ce191542b27f7f51d6b6ef778426f64d00c2b3bdc3edfb369c14f54dac6911a4"} {"question" "q-49281" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038169/state.json" "file_sha256" "294ac8a6312da67083ddee01c1c6d7e4ff3781621f176b6a7c44d36045e7e14e"} {"question" "q-49281" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038169/state.json" "file_sha256" "294ac8a6312da67083ddee01c1c6d7e4ff3781621f176b6a7c44d36045e7e14e"} {"question" "q-49281" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038169/state.json" "file_sha256" "294ac8a6312da67083ddee01c1c6d7e4ff3781621f176b6a7c44d36045e7e14e"} {"question" "q-352858" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038169/state.json" "file_sha256" "294ac8a6312da67083ddee01c1c6d7e4ff3781621f176b6a7c44d36045e7e14e"} {"question" "q-352858" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\operatorname{cot}⁡4x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThen, we use the fact that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡4x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}$ and $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡4x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=4x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u.$ \n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=4x.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ |\n\nTherefore, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(sin\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-sin\\,(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038169/state.json" "file_sha256" "294ac8a6312da67083ddee01c1c6d7e4ff3781621f176b6a7c44d36045e7e14e"} {"question" "q-352858" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038169/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ce191542b27f7f51d6b6ef778426f64d00c2b3bdc3edfb369c14f54dac6911a4"} {"question" "q-352858" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038169/state.json" "file_sha256" "294ac8a6312da67083ddee01c1c6d7e4ff3781621f176b6a7c44d36045e7e14e"} {"question" "q-352858" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038169/state.json" "file_sha256" "294ac8a6312da67083ddee01c1c6d7e4ff3781621f176b6a7c44d36045e7e14e"} {"question" "q-352868" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038169/state.json" "file_sha256" "294ac8a6312da67083ddee01c1c6d7e4ff3781621f176b6a7c44d36045e7e14e"} {"question" "q-352868" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThen, we use the fact that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}$ and $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡4x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=4x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u.$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=4x.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ |\n\nTherefore, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}(cos\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}(\\frac{1}{2}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038169/state.json" "file_sha256" "294ac8a6312da67083ddee01c1c6d7e4ff3781621f176b6a7c44d36045e7e14e"} {"question" "q-352868" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038169/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ce191542b27f7f51d6b6ef778426f64d00c2b3bdc3edfb369c14f54dac6911a4"} {"question" "q-352868" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038169/state.json" "file_sha256" "294ac8a6312da67083ddee01c1c6d7e4ff3781621f176b6a7c44d36045e7e14e"} {"question" "q-352868" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{8}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038169/state.json" "file_sha256" "294ac8a6312da67083ddee01c1c6d7e4ff3781621f176b6a7c44d36045e7e14e"}] "usage" {"q-49273" []} "basis" 1295 "retractions" [[17592186064774 :question/problem "What is $\\displaystyle \\int\\frac{\\cos^{3} x + \\cot^{2} x}{\\cos^{2} x}dx$?"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186063155 17592186063156 17592186063157 17592186063158 17592186063159] "immutable_fields" [[17592186063154 :answer-field/correct] [17592186063154 :answer-field/id] [17592186063154 :answer-field/key] [17592186063154 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
